    "body": "## Problem\n\nAll unnamed buffers currently use the same `file://` URI. When an LSP server publishes diagnostics for that URI, Neovim converts it to `/` and assigns the diagnostics to a different buffer instead of the original unnamed buffer.\n\nBecause multiple unnamed buffers also share the same URI, their diagnostics and LSP document identities cannot be kept separate.\n\n## Solution\n\nGenerate a process-local `untitled:` URI for each unnamed buffer using the Neovim process ID and buffer number.\n\nResolve these URIs back to their existing buffers when handling diagnostics, and preserve the original URI in LSP change tracking so that renaming or saving an unnamed buffer sends `didClose` for the correct document before opening the new file URI.\n\nAdd regression coverage for:\n\n- distinct and reversible URIs for unnamed buffers;\n- separate LSP `didOpen` document identities;\n- routing and clearing diagnostics in the correct unnamed buffer;\n- preserving the old and new URIs during `:saveas`.\n\nFixes #42509",
    "closed_at": null,
