            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "\r\n\r\nThe `_changetracking` part (store the didOpen URI and use it for didClose) LGTM.\r\n\r\nBlocker: `_uri_to_buf()` uses `vim.fn.bufnr(fname)` , which is wrong because `bufnr()` treats the name as a \"pattern\" and accepts partial matches. \r\nSuggestion: use `bufexists()` + `bufadd()`, which match exactly.\r\n\r\nThis will need a rebase after https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/24527 is merged. Then the `untitled:` check should use `vim.uri.parse()` .\r\n\r\nAlso is there a way to make the tests less verbose? is there an existing test that can be updated maybe?\r\n",
